**Amendment (Foundation support evidence)** · `amend:harness:foundation-closure` The green foundation gate establishes the support portion of (`gate:harness:foundation`) and (`gate:design:harness-foundation`): registry and result join, the unpublished support package and dependency-direction guard, reviewed applicable dependencies, unit/public-surface/integration levels in all four packages, real vector-runner use, bounded seeded properties and replay, owned benchmark correctness and smoke, missing-seed and correctness-failure probes, and nonverdict regression evidence. This narrows the registry and result-join probes and recorded property replay configuration of (`open:design:harness-evidence`) without closing either harness gate. An exercised replay and shrink witness, comparable baselines, independent models, and domain and client evidence remain held; shared-suite vector evidence currently covers one implementation only. The remaining foundation obligations are the complete test-site claim and obligation audit under (`gate:testing:foundation`) and tracing/observation under (`gate:observe:foundation`); performance foundation likewise awaits claims, tracing and their combined evidence. The real service tier, domain conformance suites and client harnesses remain implementation holds. No PostgreSQL or Elements service is provisioned and none is marked passed. The tokio condition awaits an actual async test; comparable benchmark campaigns remain inconclusive until reviewed baselines exist.
